From ccf369bd7941b6ca2809b0c595f9b29435443727 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:53:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bedrock): add classic Dressing Room

Import the appearance controls from viafabricplus-bedrock PR #11. Carry the native skin-rendering callback into the new appearance provider so the earlier rendering patch remains functional.

Place the subtitle and controls beneath the VFP logo without reserving space for the main screen search bar and tabs. This also gives the skin preview more vertical room at common GUI scales.

Resolve archive paths relative to a single manifest and skins.json root, including wrapped exports and nested textures. Reject traversal, duplicate entries, ambiguous roots, and oversized expanded archives before reading assets. Targeted ZIP fixtures cover nested imports and invalid roots.

Accept legacy 64x32 PNGs from file imports and pack textures. Expand each mirrored limb face into the 64x64 layout before persistence and preview, leaving modern overlays clear and preserving authored transparent hats. The face mapping matches the current Minecraft SkinTextureDownloader implementation; tests verify side-face swaps, source immutability, and file/store round trips.

Retain selected custom geometry from local Classic Skin packs, including rectangular model textures. Normalize legacy and modern geometry, reject missing models and cyclic bone hierarchies, persist the model per account, and preserve it through selection and cape edits. Login and live packets use the selected resource patch and geometry instead of silently substituting Steve. The pack and Dressing Room previews own their textures through the shared skin renderer lifecycle.
